WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.170
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.440 --> 01:34.930
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.380 --> 01:37.640
[Episode 1]

4
01:42.460 --> 01:49.350
[Ruijin, Jiangxi]

5
02:20.770 --> 02:24.460
[Mao Zedong, Chairman of the Central Executive Committee and Chairman of the Council of People's Commissars of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

6
02:44.190 --> 02:45.840
In 1931,

7
02:45.940 --> 02:48.430
the Japanese army staged the Mukden Incident,

8
02:48.430 --> 02:51.079
and occupied the three northeastern provinces of China.

9
02:51.079 --> 02:51.800
Soon after,

10
02:51.910 --> 02:55.560
they invaded Shanghai, Shanhaiguan, and Rehe,

11
02:55.620 --> 02:57.280
pushing into North China.

12
02:55.690 --> 03:01.140
[Peiping]

13
02:57.470 --> 03:01.000
The national conflict between China and Japan surpassed class struggles,

14
03:01.000 --> 03:04.200
becoming the primary contradiction in Chinese society.

15
03:04.630 --> 03:07.430
Anti-Japanese salvation movements flared up across the country.

16
03:07.430 --> 03:08.820
The Communist Party of China

17
03:08.820 --> 03:11.980
and the temporary Central Government of Chinese Soviet Republic

18
03:10.390 --> 03:14.330
[Shanghai]

19
03:12.280 --> 03:14.520
raised the banner of armed resistance,

20
03:14.800 --> 03:17.600
issuing multiple declarations and resolutions.

21
03:17.710 --> 03:20.190
In the Northeast, they formed over a dozen

22
03:20.190 --> 03:21.710
anti-Japanese guerrilla units.

23
03:21.710 --> 03:24.150
In late October 1933,

24
03:24.430 --> 03:26.520
they reached a preliminary agreement

25
03:26.520 --> 03:28.820
with the 19th Route Army, veterans of the Battle of Shanghai,

26
03:28.820 --> 03:31.380
to oppose both Japan and Chiang Kai-shek.

27
03:32.710 --> 03:34.560
Yet, amidst this national crisis,

28
03:34.560 --> 03:36.910
the Nationalist government led by Chiang Kai-shek

29
03:36.910 --> 03:38.560
stubbornly clung to the policy of

30
03:38.560 --> 03:41.400
internal pacification before external resistance.

31
03:41.400 --> 03:44.120
On May 31, 1933,

32
03:44.430 --> 03:46.400
Chiang's government and Japan

33
03:46.400 --> 03:48.150
signed the Tanggu Truce,

34
03:48.400 --> 03:50.130
leaving North China wide open.

35
03:50.680 --> 03:51.910
Later that year,

36
03:52.430 --> 03:54.430
Chiang mobilized a million troops,

37
03:54.710 --> 03:55.750
adopting a new strategy of protracted war

38
03:55.750 --> 03:57.710
and blockhouse warfare

39
03:58.079 --> 04:01.010
to encircle and suppress revolutionary base areas.

40
04:01.560 --> 04:02.220
Among them,

41
04:02.310 --> 04:03.150
half a million troops

42
04:03.150 --> 04:04.910
were deployed directly

43
04:04.960 --> 04:06.800
against the Central Soviet Area.

44
04:06.800 --> 04:08.430
Facing this formidable enemy,

45
04:08.430 --> 04:11.310
Bo Gu, head of the CPC Provisional Central Committee,

46
04:11.310 --> 04:13.150
handed the command of the Red Army

47
04:13.150 --> 04:14.910
to Li De,

48
04:14.910 --> 04:16.920
a military advisor from the Comintern.

49
04:16.920 --> 04:18.720
They completely rejected

50
04:18.920 --> 04:21.510
the correct strategies and tactics

51
04:21.600 --> 04:23.750
that Mao Zedong had used

52
04:23.750 --> 04:26.390
in previous successful Counter-Encirclement Campaigns.

53
04:26.390 --> 04:27.830
In early 1934,

54
04:28.390 --> 04:29.270
the Central Soviet Area

55
04:29.270 --> 04:31.720
was constantly squeezed and chipped away

56
04:31.720 --> 04:34.310
by the enemy's advancing blockhouses.

57
04:34.680 --> 04:36.159
The fifth Counter-Encirclement Campaign

58
04:36.159 --> 04:38.560
faced an unprecedented crisis.

59
06:01.570 --> 06:04.640
Sir, are you here for the military parade?

60
06:08.630 --> 06:09.950
The parade isn't here.

61
06:11.450 --> 06:12.930
Your hair is so long.

62
06:12.950 --> 06:14.280
Are you an opera singer?

63
06:18.730 --> 06:21.930
If I sang opera, no one would understand me.

64
06:22.630 --> 06:23.720
Run faster!

65
06:23.870 --> 06:24.270
Coming.

66
06:24.270 --> 06:24.950
Yeah.

67
06:25.630 --> 06:27.120
During the First National Soviet Congress,

68
06:27.120 --> 06:28.720
I taught him some folk songs.

69
06:28.860 --> 06:30.650
But when he sings Xingguo folk songs,

70
06:29.950 --> 06:32.070
[Xie Xingguo, Children's Corps Member]

71
06:30.700 --> 06:31.900
people from Xingguo can't understand him,

72
06:31.900 --> 06:33.830
and neither can people from Hunan.

73
06:34.490 --> 06:35.610
He is Chairman Mao.

74
06:35.870 --> 06:37.430
Chairman Mao?

75
06:38.800 --> 06:40.130
I've never heard of him.

76
06:43.500 --> 06:46.620
Xingguo, you've grown taller.

77
06:46.940 --> 06:48.070
I'm already twelve.

78
06:50.190 --> 06:52.520
During the First Congress, you were nine.

79
06:53.000 --> 06:54.230
It's been over two years.

80
06:54.230 --> 06:55.400
Have you forgotten

81
06:55.590 --> 06:56.600
the characters I taught you?

82
06:56.600 --> 06:57.360
No.

83
06:57.690 --> 06:59.620
I've even learned a lot of new ones.

84
07:00.750 --> 07:03.040
Then do you recognize these?

85
07:04.360 --> 07:05.270
Of course.

86
07:06.860 --> 07:11.530
Treading on the martyrs' bloodstains

87
07:12.370 --> 07:13.820
to advance!

88
07:14.460 --> 07:16.020
I know them all!

89
07:27.640 --> 07:28.470
Fall in!

90
07:29.060 --> 07:29.990
Line up quickly!

91
07:30.430 --> 07:31.160
At ease!

92
07:31.450 --> 07:31.970
Hurry up!

93
07:31.970 --> 07:32.650
Attention!

94
07:32.670 --> 07:33.500
Kid,

95
07:33.720 --> 07:35.780
who made these straw sandals for you?

96
07:36.310 --> 07:37.430
My dad made them.

97
07:38.230 --> 07:39.159
They're too big.

98
07:39.430 --> 07:40.690
You're still growing.

99
07:40.750 --> 07:42.360
You'll grow into them soon enough.

100
07:42.360 --> 07:43.000
Eight.

101
07:43.310 --> 07:43.920
Nine.

102
07:44.430 --> 07:46.000
Xie Xingguo, fall in!

103
07:46.190 --> 07:46.830
Coming!

104
07:49.720 --> 07:51.120
Eyes right!

105
07:52.920 --> 07:53.560
One!

106
07:54.210 --> 07:55.000
Kill!

107
07:55.390 --> 07:56.159
Two!

108
07:57.240 --> 07:57.870
One!

109
07:57.870 --> 07:58.870
Kill!

110
07:59.040 --> 07:59.750
Two!

111
08:00.560 --> 08:01.070
One!

112
08:01.070 --> 08:02.000
Kill!

113
08:02.310 --> 08:03.120
Two!

114
08:03.950 --> 08:04.510
One!

115
08:04.600 --> 08:05.270
Kill!

116
08:05.750 --> 08:06.630
Two!

117
08:07.360 --> 08:08.110
One!

118
08:08.240 --> 08:09.160
Kill!

119
08:09.240 --> 08:10.160
Two!

120
08:11.160 --> 08:11.920
One!

121
08:11.950 --> 08:12.680
Kill!

122
08:13.070 --> 08:13.950
Two!

123
08:15.160 --> 08:15.680
One!

124
08:15.870 --> 08:16.680
Kill!

125
08:16.920 --> 08:17.920
Two!

126
08:18.920 --> 08:19.480
One!

127
08:19.480 --> 08:20.190
Kill!

128
08:20.310 --> 08:21.120
Two!

129
08:21.800 --> 08:22.190
One!

130
08:22.580 --> 08:28.750
[Shazhouba, Ruijin, Jiangxi]

131
08:28.770 --> 08:30.550
[Li De, Comintern Military Advisor]

132
08:33.630 --> 08:35.120
That one.

133
08:35.520 --> 08:36.679
[Bo Gu (Qin Bangxian), Head of the CPC Central Committee]

134
08:37.000 --> 08:38.510
Catch that one!

135
09:03.150 --> 09:04.010
Comrade Enlai.

136
09:07.380 --> 09:09.480
[Zhou Enlai, Member of the CPC Politburo Standing Committee and General Political Commissar of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

137
09:08.670 --> 09:09.750
Comrade Li De.

138
09:10.240 --> 09:11.030
Zhou Enlai,

139
09:11.390 --> 09:13.440
what brings you here?

140
09:13.960 --> 09:15.150
The Nationalist army

141
09:15.150 --> 09:16.390
has once again launched a massive offensive

142
09:16.390 --> 09:18.510
against the Hunan-Jiangxi Soviet Area.

143
09:18.510 --> 09:20.030
The situation is critical.

144
09:20.030 --> 09:21.910
Have you reviewed

145
09:21.960 --> 09:23.310
the plan for the Counter-Encirclement Campaign

146
09:23.310 --> 09:24.710
drafted by the comrades?

147
09:24.840 --> 09:27.080
Have you read their plan for Counter-Encirclement Campaign?

148
09:27.080 --> 09:30.440
I don't need to read this plan.

149
09:28.790 --> 09:32.300
[Wu Xiuquan, Translator]

150
09:30.440 --> 09:32.670
The Hunan-Jiangxi Soviet Area must follow my guidelines

151
09:32.670 --> 09:34.790
to formulate their operation plan.

152
09:35.030 --> 09:37.440
Not a single word is to be altered.

153
09:37.440 --> 09:38.670
... to formulate their operation plan.

154
09:38.670 --> 09:40.120
Not a single word is to be altered.

155
09:40.120 --> 09:42.790
The Hunan-Jiangxi Soviet Area has its own practical problems.

156
09:42.790 --> 09:46.190
The Hunan-Jiangxi Soviet Area has its own practical problems.

157
09:46.190 --> 09:48.590
If they think they know best,

158
09:48.620 --> 09:50.220
then what do they need

159
09:50.470 --> 09:53.350
a military advisor for?

160
09:53.390 --> 09:54.480
... then what do they need

161
09:54.480 --> 09:55.810
a military advisor for?

162
10:01.150 --> 10:02.360
They're

163
10:03.600 --> 10:04.630
so nice.

164
10:05.360 --> 10:06.480
Little ducks.

165
10:12.790 --> 10:15.600
What are you still doing there? Let's go.

166
10:15.750 --> 10:17.950
Alright, stop catching them. Let's go.

167
10:22.150 --> 10:23.480
You two young comrades,

168
10:23.670 --> 10:24.600
don't come over!

169
10:24.850 --> 10:26.180
Walk on the ridge!

170
10:26.960 --> 10:28.690
Careful not to prick your feet!

171
10:29.240 --> 10:30.150
Comrade Enlai,

172
10:30.810 --> 10:32.240
I need a word with you.

173
10:33.550 --> 10:34.320
Go ahead.

174
10:34.750 --> 10:36.870
During the first Executive Committee meeting

175
10:36.870 --> 10:38.750
after the Second National Soviet Congress,

176
10:38.750 --> 10:39.910
I'd like to nominate Comrade Luofu

177
10:39.910 --> 10:42.840
for Chairman of the Council of People's Commissars.

178
10:42.870 --> 10:45.030
Comrade Mao Zedong

179
10:45.210 --> 10:46.540
only needs to serve as

180
10:46.570 --> 10:48.250
Chairman of the Central Executive Committee.

181
10:48.250 --> 10:49.310
Is that necessary?

182
10:49.720 --> 10:50.820
Comrade Mao Zedong

183
10:51.500 --> 10:54.390
doesn't manage the daily affairs of the government.

184
10:54.390 --> 10:56.600
He'd make a fine Kalinin of the Soviet.

185
10:56.790 --> 10:59.320
I've also discussed this with some Politburo members.

186
10:59.320 --> 11:01.580
Find a chance to let him know beforehand,

187
11:02.000 --> 11:04.670
just so he's prepared.

188
11:15.110 --> 11:19.240
[The whole world is unified]

189
11:47.000 --> 11:49.750
[Chen Geng, President of the First Infantry School of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

190
11:59.380 --> 12:01.270
[Zhu De, Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission and Commander-in-Chief of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

191
12:17.890 --> 12:22.970
[Station of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

192
12:25.130 --> 12:27.320
[Qian Zhuangfei, Deputy Director of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

193
12:28.790 --> 12:29.670
Is it this one?

194
12:29.830 --> 12:31.620
Not this one, no.

195
12:34.790 --> 12:38.640
[Zeng Xisheng, Director of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

196
12:41.840 --> 12:42.630
I got it!

197
13:10.120 --> 13:11.270
Comrade Enlai,

198
13:12.130 --> 13:13.190
why hasn't Mao Zedong arrived yet?

199
13:13.190 --> 13:14.120
What's going on?

200
13:19.550 --> 13:20.480
Comrade Zedong.

201
13:28.630 --> 13:29.440
Let's begin.

202
13:30.790 --> 13:32.430
The Congress now begins!

203
13:32.790 --> 13:35.200
I now invite Comrade Bo Gu to speak.

204
13:45.200 --> 13:46.240
Comrades,

205
13:46.670 --> 13:48.120
this military parade is

206
13:48.670 --> 13:50.510
the opening ceremony of our Second

207
13:50.510 --> 13:54.320
National Congress of the Chinese Soviet.

208
13:54.790 --> 13:55.790
First of all,

209
13:56.000 --> 13:58.320
I would like to extend a warm welcome

210
13:58.710 --> 14:00.190
to all the delegates,

211
14:00.460 --> 14:01.660
workers and peasants

212
14:02.010 --> 14:04.420
attending the parade.

213
14:04.480 --> 14:06.910
Great!

214
14:16.480 --> 14:18.320
And I send my regards

215
14:18.840 --> 14:21.550
to the Red Army commanders, fighters, Red Guards,

216
14:21.550 --> 14:24.280
and Children's Corps members in the march-past.

217
14:30.000 --> 14:31.360
The Nationalist Central Army

218
14:31.360 --> 14:33.620
took Quanzhou and Zhangzhou yesterday.

219
14:33.960 --> 14:35.760
The Fujian Incident has failed.

220
14:36.630 --> 14:37.230
We have...

221
14:37.380 --> 14:40.380
[Xiang Ying, Secretary of the Central Secretariat and Vice Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

222
14:37.550 --> 14:38.240
I didn't expect it to happen so fast.

223
14:38.240 --> 14:39.750
... representatives of workers and peasants

224
14:39.750 --> 14:41.910
from Nationalist-controlled areas,

225
14:44.000 --> 14:45.130
representatives of

226
14:45.660 --> 14:47.330
the People's Revolutionary Army

227
14:47.330 --> 14:50.000
fighting a brutal national revolutionary war

228
14:50.000 --> 14:52.030
against Japanese imperialism,

229
14:52.200 --> 14:54.510
and representatives from colonies

230
14:54.510 --> 14:55.670
oppressed by various imperialists.

231
14:55.670 --> 14:56.790
What's wrong?

232
14:56.720 --> 15:00.240
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian), Member of the CPC Politburo Standing Committee]

233
14:57.240 --> 14:58.640
Your arrival proves that

234
14:58.750 --> 15:01.320
the Soviet movement

235
15:01.360 --> 15:03.870
is not only the sole path to liberation

236
15:04.360 --> 15:07.960
for the vast working masses of China...

237
15:07.960 --> 15:10.320
With no allies, standing alone

238
15:10.870 --> 15:12.330
and fighting recklessly,

239
15:13.120 --> 15:14.580
we will find our situation

240
15:15.630 --> 15:17.120
only getting tougher.

241
15:17.720 --> 15:18.670
... the path to liberation...

242
15:18.670 --> 15:21.720
I fear if they fall, we're next.

243
15:22.390 --> 15:24.360
Comrades, I believe...

244
15:24.440 --> 15:25.270
Mao,

245
15:26.120 --> 15:28.240
if we had listened to you

246
15:28.600 --> 15:31.080
and honored the preliminary agreement

247
15:31.440 --> 15:33.600
signed with the Fujian side,

248
15:33.870 --> 15:35.800
things wouldn't have come to this.

249
15:36.670 --> 15:40.000
... can be greatly expanded and developed!

250
15:40.720 --> 15:44.080
We will plant the red flag all over China!

251
15:44.080 --> 15:46.720
Well said!

252
15:48.870 --> 15:51.910
We will hold a parade in Nanjing, Shanghai,

253
15:52.270 --> 15:54.000
and Wuchang!

254
15:54.510 --> 15:57.510
We will hold our

255
15:57.750 --> 16:01.910
Third National Soviet Congress there!

256
16:01.910 --> 16:05.030
Well said!

257
16:36.510 --> 16:38.270
Bo Gu, Comrade Enlai,

258
16:39.750 --> 16:42.610
I've finished writing the report for the Congress.

259
16:43.390 --> 16:44.600
When it's my turn to speak,

260
16:44.600 --> 16:47.720
I might need a bit more time.

261
16:51.790 --> 16:52.720
Let's continue.

262
16:56.720 --> 17:00.080
The march-past begins now!

263
17:09.720 --> 17:11.640
Shoulder arms!

264
17:15.829 --> 17:17.790
Forward march!

265
17:20.400 --> 17:22.069
One, two, one.

266
17:22.510 --> 17:24.200
One, two, one.

267
17:24.589 --> 17:26.200
One, two, one.

268
17:26.720 --> 17:28.240
One, two, one.

269
17:29.030 --> 17:30.720
Eyes right!

270
17:31.240 --> 17:33.000
Long live the Red Army!

271
17:33.200 --> 17:35.070
Long live the Red Army!

272
17:35.290 --> 17:36.970
Long live the Soviet!

273
17:37.000 --> 17:38.890
Long live the Soviet!

274
17:38.920 --> 17:41.310
Long live Communist Party of China!

275
17:41.310 --> 17:43.960
Long live the Communist Party of China!

276
17:44.200 --> 17:45.830
Eyes front!

277
17:46.640 --> 17:48.240
Eyes right!

278
17:48.830 --> 17:50.550
Long live the Red Army!

279
17:51.000 --> 17:52.920
Long live the Red Army!

280
17:53.750 --> 17:55.640
Long live the Soviet!

281
17:55.750 --> 17:57.680
Long live the Soviet!

282
17:57.920 --> 17:59.640
Long live the Communist Party of China!

283
17:58.100 --> 17:59.450
[Li Zhuoran, Director of the Political Department of the 1st Red Army Corps]

284
17:59.640 --> 18:03.200
Long live the Communist Party of China!

285
18:18.100 --> 18:20.540
Long live the Red Army!

286
18:20.880 --> 18:25.240
Long live the Soviet!

287
18:25.350 --> 18:27.270
Long live the Communist Party of China!

288
18:27.270 --> 18:30.480
Long live the Communist Party of China!

289
18:30.640 --> 18:32.470
Eyes right!

290
18:32.720 --> 18:34.590
Long live the Red Army!

291
18:34.750 --> 18:36.720
Long live the Red Army!

292
18:36.880 --> 18:38.640
Long live the Soviet!

293
18:38.640 --> 18:40.750
Long live the Soviet!

294
18:40.960 --> 18:43.160
Long live the Communist Party of China!

295
18:43.310 --> 18:45.830
Long live the Communist Party of China!

296
18:46.200 --> 18:50.400
Long live the Red Army!

297
18:50.680 --> 18:52.920
Long live the Communist Party of China!

298
18:53.070 --> 18:56.720
Long live the Communist Party of China!

299
18:57.000 --> 19:01.820
[Nanchang Headquarters, Nanchang, Jiangxi]

300
18:58.790 --> 19:00.160
The Fujian crisis is resolved.

301
19:00.160 --> 19:02.270
Your greatest concern did not happen.

302
19:02.270 --> 19:04.240
Now we can focus our efforts

303
19:04.440 --> 19:06.070
on dealing with the Zhu-Mao communist forces.

304
19:06.070 --> 19:07.070
Besides that,

305
19:07.260 --> 19:08.900
you also need to take the long view,

306
19:08.900 --> 19:11.160
and use the anti-communist campaign to weaken the warlords,

307
19:11.160 --> 19:12.770
and quickly put an end to the situation

308
19:12.770 --> 19:13.420
where various warlords rule their own domains

309
19:13.420 --> 19:14.790
with their own agendas.

310
19:15.040 --> 19:17.070
So this is your strategy of driving the tiger to swallow the wolf?

311
19:17.070 --> 19:17.750
Exactly.

312
19:18.070 --> 19:19.400
Weakening the warlords

313
19:19.590 --> 19:21.790
is also a way of pacifying the interior.

314
19:21.940 --> 19:22.920
Centralization, unification,

315
19:22.920 --> 19:23.960
and establishing order,

316
19:23.960 --> 19:26.480
This is the ultimate foundation for resisting foreign aggression.

317
19:26.480 --> 19:29.210
Starting today, the New Life Movement Promotion Association is established.

318
19:29.210 --> 19:30.680
I shall serve as its president.

319
19:30.680 --> 19:32.680
With propriety, justice, honesty, and honor as our guiding principles,

320
19:32.680 --> 19:34.030
we launch the New Life Movement.

321
19:34.030 --> 19:34.940
Generalissimo,

322
19:34.940 --> 19:37.740
our army has surrounded the Communist Central Base Area.

323
19:37.740 --> 19:39.510
Across Jiangxi province,

324
19:39.550 --> 19:42.290
we have built over 6,000 blockhouses, fortresses, bridgeheads,

325
19:42.290 --> 19:45.130
road-protection forts, and fortified villages.

326
19:45.070 --> 19:48.230
[He Guoguang, Director of the First Department, Nanchang Headquarters]

327
19:45.160 --> 19:48.240
We have completed the military encirclement of the communist forces.

328
19:48.240 --> 19:49.200
According to the established plan,

329
19:49.200 --> 19:51.160
our forces will continue to impose

330
19:51.200 --> 19:53.070
economic, transportation, and communication blockades

331
19:53.070 --> 19:54.830
across the entire Jiangxi communist area.

332
19:54.830 --> 19:57.270
They will not receive a single grain of rice or drop of water,

333
19:57.270 --> 19:58.920
nor will any news slip through.

334
19:58.920 --> 19:59.510
This way,

335
19:59.550 --> 20:02.160
the communist forces and the civilians will be increasingly severed.

336
20:02.160 --> 20:02.960
Isolated and helpless,

337
20:02.960 --> 20:04.830
they will be like fish out of water, or turtles in a jar.

338
20:04.830 --> 20:05.830
Once our grand army advances,

339
20:05.830 --> 20:07.270
we will wipe them out in one fell swoop.

340
20:07.270 --> 20:08.160
Gentlemen,

341
20:08.680 --> 20:12.910
[Chiang Kai-shek, Generalissimo of the Military Affairs Commission of the Nationalist Government]

342
20:10.630 --> 20:13.110
ninety miles is but half of a hundred-mile journey.

343
20:13.110 --> 20:14.960
The closer we are to success,

344
20:15.800 --> 20:17.730
the less we can afford to slack off.

345
20:17.740 --> 20:21.070
The New Life Movement holds significant practical meaning

346
20:21.240 --> 20:22.960
just like internal pacification before external resistance.

347
20:22.820 --> 20:24.920
[Chen Cheng, Frontline Commander-in-Chief of the Northern Route Army and Commander of the 3rd Route Army]

348
20:23.550 --> 20:25.150
As revolutionary soldiers,

349
20:25.310 --> 20:27.010
we must correct hypocrisy with solid action,

350
20:27.010 --> 20:28.590
correct laziness with swift action,

351
20:28.590 --> 20:30.360
and correct cowardice with tough action.

352
20:30.360 --> 20:31.810
[Yan Daogang, Director of the Attendants' Office of the Generalissimo of the Military Affairs Commission]

353
20:30.790 --> 20:31.980
Should anyone else ever

354
20:31.980 --> 20:33.200
[Wu Qiwei, Commander of the 7th Column, Northern Route Army]

355
20:32.110 --> 20:33.790
act like the 19th Route Army in Fujian,

356
20:33.250 --> 20:34.300
[Zhou Hunyuan, Commander of the 8th Column, Northern Route Army]

357
20:33.790 --> 20:35.550
using the pretext of marching north to resist Japan

358
20:34.340 --> 20:35.430
[Xue Yue, Commander-in-Chief of the 6th Route Army, Northern Route Army]

359
20:35.750 --> 20:37.330
to avoid actively suppressing the communists,

360
20:37.330 --> 20:40.260
they shall be charged with cowardice and desertion,

361
20:40.530 --> 20:42.320
and executed without mercy.

362
20:42.410 --> 20:43.300
Yes.

363
20:48.270 --> 20:49.720
Today, standing here with you gentlemen,

364
20:49.720 --> 20:51.720
looking out from this great height...

365
20:51.720 --> 20:54.320
all the other peaks truly seem insignificant!

366
21:11.900 --> 21:14.900
[Eastern Front Defensive Positions, Central Soviet Area]

367
22:44.320 --> 22:47.500
[Ruijin, Jiangxi]

368
22:46.160 --> 22:46.960
Come here!

369
22:48.110 --> 22:49.370
Come on, get over here!

370
22:50.240 --> 22:51.070
It's okay.

371
22:52.480 --> 22:53.410
Don't be afraid.

372
22:53.960 --> 22:54.890
It'll pass soon.

373
22:55.270 --> 22:56.270
Come on, this way.

374
23:05.400 --> 23:07.480
Comrades, don't panic.

375
23:07.790 --> 23:10.440
Enemy air raids on the Central Soviet Area are common.

376
23:10.440 --> 23:11.200
Take it easy.

377
23:11.350 --> 23:12.750
Move inside!

378
23:12.830 --> 23:14.480
Don't panic! Don't panic!

379
23:16.590 --> 23:17.400
Don't push!

380
23:17.510 --> 23:18.400
Stop pushing!

381
23:28.480 --> 23:29.270
Don't push!

382
23:30.200 --> 23:31.170
Wait a minute!

383
23:35.920 --> 23:37.720
We have to come in here every day.

384
23:42.920 --> 23:43.720
Get over here!

385
24:03.680 --> 24:04.550
Who is it?

386
24:07.310 --> 24:08.200
Who patted me?

387
24:08.510 --> 24:10.240
Spread out, everyone!

388
24:10.480 --> 24:10.960
Get in quickly!

389
24:10.960 --> 24:11.540
Move inside, inside!

390
24:11.540 --> 24:12.680
Comrades in front, speed up a bit!

391
24:12.680 --> 24:13.590
Comrades, move inside!

392
24:13.590 --> 24:14.480
Squeeze in!

393
24:14.790 --> 24:15.270
Here.

394
24:15.510 --> 24:17.640
Comrades, don't panic!

395
24:17.640 --> 24:18.550
Move to the sides!

396
24:18.550 --> 24:20.070
Move inside!

397
24:20.880 --> 24:21.550
Don't panic!

398
24:21.550 --> 24:22.830
Don't panic!

399
24:22.830 --> 24:23.560
Move inside!

400
24:23.680 --> 24:24.480
Don't panic!

401
24:24.750 --> 24:26.720
Split to both sides!

402
24:26.960 --> 24:28.110
Go left!

403
24:28.110 --> 24:29.350
There are comrades ahead!

404
24:29.350 --> 24:29.960
Move inside!

405
24:29.960 --> 24:30.820
Comrade Enlai.

406
24:30.960 --> 24:32.000
Comrade Enlai.

407
24:32.830 --> 24:33.480
Over here!

408
24:34.400 --> 24:36.000
Squeeze inside! Squeeze in!

409
24:36.510 --> 24:37.200
Thank you!

410
24:37.200 --> 24:37.750
Quick!

411
24:37.750 --> 24:39.280
Comrades, move further in!

412
24:40.400 --> 24:41.790
Squeeze in!

413
24:43.140 --> 24:44.010
Mao.

414
24:46.200 --> 24:47.730
It's alright. Don't panic.

415
24:47.960 --> 24:49.000
Let me through.

416
24:49.720 --> 24:50.520
Chairman Mao.

417
24:51.700 --> 24:52.200
Commander-in-Chief.

418
24:52.200 --> 24:52.830
Wang Zhen.

419
24:53.720 --> 24:54.550
Chairman Mao,

420
24:54.880 --> 24:56.490
I'd like to ask for your advice

421
24:56.490 --> 24:59.880
[Wang Zhen, Political Commissar of the 17th Red Division]

422
24:56.720 --> 24:58.640
regarding the Hunan-Jiangxi Soviet Area's plan

423
24:58.640 --> 25:00.770
for Counter-Encirclement Campaign.

424
25:03.720 --> 25:05.720
I'm no longer in charge of military command.

425
25:05.720 --> 25:07.030
Go find that man.

426
25:08.200 --> 25:09.530
The pipe-smoking Li De.

427
25:10.350 --> 25:12.210
He doesn't even read our reports.

428
25:12.470 --> 25:14.820
He expects us to fight

429
25:14.840 --> 25:17.350
exactly according to his written directives.

430
25:17.350 --> 25:18.400
Let me see.

431
25:19.950 --> 25:21.590
Let's have a look. Looking won't hurt.

432
25:21.590 --> 25:22.200
Here.

433
25:23.800 --> 25:24.860
In this directive,

434
25:25.000 --> 25:28.140
he even drew the exact locations and dimensions of the blockhouses,

435
25:28.140 --> 25:30.830
but he's never even been to Hunan-Jiangxi province!

436
25:30.830 --> 25:33.690
Blockhouse warfare and wars of attrition again...

437
25:33.720 --> 25:35.680
How many men and guns do you have?

438
25:35.790 --> 25:37.880
Can you withstand the Nationalists' planes and artillery?

439
25:37.880 --> 25:39.200
I expressed my doubts too,

440
25:39.200 --> 25:40.400
but Comrade Li De said

441
25:40.770 --> 25:43.480
this is the experience the Soviet Red Army paid for in blood,

442
25:43.480 --> 25:45.510
and we must respect and follow it.

443
25:45.960 --> 25:47.960
We respect their experience

444
25:47.960 --> 25:49.490
that they paid for in blood,

445
25:49.530 --> 25:50.950
but we must respect even more

446
25:50.950 --> 25:53.350
the experience we paid for in our own blood.

447
25:57.270 --> 25:59.100
Engaging the enemy beyond our borders

448
25:59.100 --> 26:01.500
and fighting a blockhouse war against them

449
26:01.580 --> 26:03.380
is either cowardly or arrogant.

450
26:03.660 --> 26:05.990
Cowardice is rightist, and arrogance is leftist.

451
26:05.990 --> 26:07.270
The Chinese revolution

452
26:07.270 --> 26:09.470
can neither afford to go left nor right.

453
26:12.000 --> 26:12.880
Take it easy.

454
26:16.750 --> 26:18.440
Didn't you use to drive trains?

455
26:18.440 --> 26:19.440
You know how it is.

456
26:19.670 --> 26:21.300
When a train is moving forward,

457
26:21.300 --> 26:22.880
you switch tracks when you need to.

458
26:22.880 --> 26:24.480
You need to be the switchmen.

459
26:24.720 --> 26:27.310
The Hunan-Jiangxi troops need to stay mobile.

460
26:27.310 --> 26:28.640
Concentrate your forces,

461
26:28.640 --> 26:29.940
target the enemy's weak points,

462
26:29.940 --> 26:31.680
and fight wars of annihilation.

463
26:31.680 --> 26:33.400
That's what you're best at.

464
26:36.550 --> 26:39.010
Alright. After I get back,

465
26:39.350 --> 26:40.830
I'll report this to Comrade Ren Bishi.

466
26:40.830 --> 26:41.750
Okay.

467
26:42.650 --> 26:44.010
Excuse me, coming through!

468
26:44.010 --> 26:44.830
Sorry, it's urgent!

469
26:44.830 --> 26:45.880
Excuse me, coming through!

470
26:45.880 --> 26:46.590
Chairman.

471
26:46.830 --> 26:47.510
Chen Geng.

472
26:47.680 --> 26:48.440
Someone submitted a report

473
26:48.440 --> 26:50.720
to Wang Jiaxiang, Director of the General Political Department,

474
26:50.720 --> 26:53.120
demanding the execution of Xiao Jinguang.

475
26:55.680 --> 26:58.240
Should we talk to Li De about it?

476
27:02.680 --> 27:05.240
Is Wang Jiaxiang the Director of the General Political Department?

477
27:05.240 --> 27:05.880
Is he?

478
27:05.880 --> 27:06.480
Yes.

479
27:09.270 --> 27:10.920
I'll go to him right now.

480
27:11.310 --> 27:11.920
Wait...

481
27:11.920 --> 27:12.510
Mao, Mao!

482
27:12.510 --> 27:13.170
Where is he?

483
27:13.350 --> 27:15.280
The all-clear hasn't sounded yet!

484
27:17.430 --> 27:18.280
I just...

485
27:18.790 --> 27:21.110
I just saw Director Wang over there.

486
27:37.550 --> 27:39.240
Take care.

487
27:39.510 --> 27:40.570
Comrade Jiaxiang!

488
27:43.030 --> 27:43.960
Comrade Zedong.

489
27:44.270 --> 27:46.510
I heard someone wrote a report to you,

490
27:46.740 --> 27:48.600
asking to execute Xiao Jinguang.

491
27:48.980 --> 27:51.160
[Wang Jiaxiang, Vice Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission and Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Red Army]

492
27:49.480 --> 27:50.240
Yes.

493
27:50.680 --> 27:53.240
Xiao Jinguang's case was settled long ago.

494
27:53.440 --> 27:55.270
He shouldn't have been held responsible

495
27:55.270 --> 27:58.160
for the fall of Lichuan and the defeat at Huwan.

496
27:58.400 --> 28:00.160
Why must they put him to death?

497
28:00.310 --> 28:03.160
Mao, you can read the writing on the wall.

498
28:03.590 --> 28:04.720
Their whole routine

499
28:04.880 --> 28:06.160
is just like how they criticized Luo Ming last year,

500
28:06.160 --> 28:07.920
and criticized Deng, Mao, Xie, and Gu.

501
28:07.920 --> 28:09.180
It's exactly the same.

502
28:11.350 --> 28:13.980
Are they using Xiao Jinguang to target me?

503
28:14.640 --> 28:16.940
I already have three labels pinned on my head:

504
28:16.940 --> 28:18.800
Marxism in the mountain valleys,

505
28:19.650 --> 28:21.260
right-leaning conservatism,

506
28:21.260 --> 28:22.680
and the rich peasant line.

507
28:22.680 --> 28:24.480
My name has already been dragged through the mud.

508
28:24.480 --> 28:25.270
Why bother?

509
28:25.550 --> 28:28.110
Why drag Xiao Jinguang down just to get at me?

510
28:28.400 --> 28:29.330
Comrade Zedong,

511
28:29.730 --> 28:31.170
I completely disagree

512
28:32.260 --> 28:33.980
with their whole routine.

513
28:34.550 --> 28:37.300
After helping command the 4th Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

514
28:37.300 --> 28:38.130
I am no longer

515
28:38.650 --> 28:40.820
the Wang Jiaxiang I used to be.

516
28:41.270 --> 28:42.720
The first three Counter-Encirclement Campaigns

517
28:42.720 --> 28:44.510
were commanded by you.

518
28:44.990 --> 28:46.480
In the 4th Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

519
28:46.480 --> 28:49.240
even though they didn't use you,

520
28:49.310 --> 28:51.510
they still used your old strategies.

521
28:51.790 --> 28:52.920
And they still won.

522
28:53.400 --> 28:54.400
But look at us now,

523
28:54.830 --> 28:56.250
all military command

524
28:56.680 --> 28:58.540
listens to that foreign advisor.

525
28:59.440 --> 29:00.790
And what's the result?

526
29:01.310 --> 29:02.370
Comrade Jiaxiang,

527
29:02.790 --> 29:04.920
you're much more clear-headed than those

528
29:04.920 --> 29:07.520
who can only see the foreign advisor's dogmas.

529
29:07.680 --> 29:09.440
They only see dogma,

530
29:09.550 --> 29:13.050
but they can't see Chiang Kai-shek's blockhouses and barbed wire.

531
29:13.050 --> 29:14.510
So about Xiao Jinguang...

532
29:14.790 --> 29:16.320
how do you plan to handle it?

533
29:18.750 --> 29:19.350
I...

534
29:22.480 --> 29:23.480
All-clear!

535
29:24.350 --> 29:25.160
All-clear!

536
29:25.160 --> 29:25.960
It's cleared.

537
29:27.590 --> 29:28.920
The all-clear sounded!

538
29:29.750 --> 29:30.680
Everyone, evacuate in an orderly manner!

539
29:30.680 --> 29:32.110
Orderly evacuation!

540
29:32.110 --> 29:34.030
Don't push!

541
29:34.240 --> 29:35.240
You can go out now.

542
29:35.960 --> 29:36.960
Everyone, stop pushing!

543
29:36.960 --> 29:37.550
Comrade Jiaxiang.

544
29:37.550 --> 29:39.500
Commander-in-Chief, urgent report from the front!

545
29:39.500 --> 29:40.550
There's an emergency!

546
29:40.550 --> 29:41.520
Don't panic!

547
29:44.400 --> 29:45.270
The all-clear sounded!

548
29:45.270 --> 29:46.030
Comrade Jiaxiang!

549
29:46.030 --> 29:46.550
The all-clear sounded!

550
29:46.550 --> 29:47.370
Don't push!

551
29:49.790 --> 29:50.590
Don't push!

552
29:50.590 --> 29:51.790
Comrades, slow down!

553
29:53.140 --> 29:54.200
Comrade Jiaxiang!

554
29:54.480 --> 29:55.160
Let's go.

555
29:56.720 --> 29:57.920
Comrade Li De,

556
29:58.090 --> 29:59.590
regarding Comrade Xiao Jinguang's case,

557
29:59.590 --> 30:00.850
I reiterate my stance.

558
30:01.310 --> 30:03.460
As Director of the General Political Department,

559
30:03.460 --> 30:04.700
I will not sign it!

560
30:05.960 --> 30:08.220
-Comrade Jiaxiang. -Comrade Jiaxiang.

561
30:08.830 --> 30:10.040
Comrade Jiaxiang.

562
30:17.680 --> 30:20.350
This isn't the right place to discuss this.

563
30:20.820 --> 30:22.820
Can we discuss it in a meeting later?

564
30:26.400 --> 30:27.010
Okay.

565
30:35.100 --> 30:35.960
Comrade Enlai,

566
30:46.920 --> 30:48.050
did you talk with Mao

567
30:48.240 --> 30:50.070
about what we discussed earlier?

568
30:50.070 --> 30:50.830
Not yet.

569
30:51.220 --> 30:52.620
Why haven't you told him?

570
30:53.390 --> 30:54.280
Comrade Bo Gu,

571
30:55.280 --> 30:58.470
shouldn't we be more cautious with this decision?

572
31:06.960 --> 31:09.880
Comrade Enlai, this matter...

573
32:20.920 --> 32:26.070
...to celebrate the successful opening of the Second National Soviet Congress.

574
32:26.200 --> 32:28.270
Good evening, delegates!

575
32:28.920 --> 32:31.480
Please enjoy our first performance,

576
32:31.480 --> 32:33.030
a Soviet dance:

577
32:33.480 --> 32:35.510
The Soldier's Dance!

578
32:36.110 --> 32:37.790
Great!

579
32:50.550 --> 32:51.750
A Soviet dance?

580
32:52.030 --> 32:52.830
Right.

581
32:55.070 --> 32:58.000
It depicts the combat and daily life of the soldiers.

582
33:02.480 --> 33:06.200
The Nationalist army has split into three columns

583
33:06.310 --> 33:10.590
and launched a new offensive against the Central Soviet Area.

584
33:10.870 --> 33:14.060
We have decided to shorten the agenda of the Second Congress

585
33:14.060 --> 33:17.450
and conclude it ahead of schedule.

586
33:18.030 --> 33:20.790
That is necessary.

587
33:21.590 --> 33:23.770
Regarding military deployment,

588
33:23.800 --> 33:26.920
are there any new plans?

589
33:27.240 --> 33:29.790
New plans? No.

590
33:30.400 --> 33:33.590
The correct operational guidelines will not change.

591
33:34.070 --> 33:37.880
The Red Army should fight regular warfare,

592
33:38.480 --> 33:41.960
using the short, swift thrust tactics

593
33:41.960 --> 33:44.270
that proved effective on the Soviet battlefields.

594
33:44.270 --> 33:45.750
Position against position.

595
33:45.750 --> 33:47.640
Fight blockhouse against blockhouse.

596
33:47.640 --> 33:50.270
Engage the enemy beyond the borders.

597
33:50.270 --> 33:52.880
We must not waver.

598
33:53.030 --> 33:57.200
We will continue to use blockhouse and positional warfare,

599
33:57.480 --> 33:58.680
and actively employ short, swift thrust tactics.

600
33:58.680 --> 34:00.200
Great!

601
34:04.640 --> 34:06.440
We will not allow a single

602
34:04.660 --> 34:07.140
[Deng Yingchao, Secretary of the CPC Politburo]

603
34:06.440 --> 34:09.400
Nationalist soldier into the Central Soviet Area!

604
34:10.190 --> 34:11.840
This plan is feasible.

605
34:13.550 --> 34:14.800
Great!

606
34:16.460 --> 34:18.330
[He Zizhen, Mao Zedong's wife]

607
34:20.840 --> 34:24.920
I heard that during the Congress,

608
34:24.920 --> 34:26.480
Mao brought up his usual

609
34:26.480 --> 34:28.610
guerrilla tactics to disrupt morale.

610
34:29.710 --> 34:32.110
Great!

611
34:32.920 --> 34:34.030
I am aware of this.

612
34:34.580 --> 34:36.510
He is the Chairman of the Soviet Government,

613
34:36.510 --> 34:38.440
not the Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission.

614
34:38.440 --> 34:40.440
This is a sign of his contempt for us.

615
34:40.830 --> 34:43.080
Comrade Li De, please calm down.

616
34:43.199 --> 34:45.600
After all, we are making the big decisions.

617
34:45.670 --> 34:48.870
Mao may make mistakes on big issues, but not on small ones.

618
34:48.920 --> 34:53.070
He does have working ability.

619
34:53.230 --> 34:55.670
This was also acknowledged by Comrade Wang Ming.

620
34:55.670 --> 34:57.550
Are you questioning my ability?

621
34:57.710 --> 34:59.070
No, no.

622
34:59.440 --> 35:03.400
I'm saying that how we treat Mao

623
35:03.400 --> 35:06.530
shouldn't be the same as how we treat ordinary comrades.

624
35:08.800 --> 35:11.150
Great!

625
35:12.070 --> 35:13.630
Great!

626
35:13.630 --> 35:16.710
Great!

627
35:17.320 --> 35:20.400
Great!

628
35:23.320 --> 35:25.710
Mao's problem lies here:

629
35:25.920 --> 35:29.070
his mind lacks Marxism-Leninism,

630
35:29.280 --> 35:31.590
and he reeks of traditional old Chinese culture,

631
35:31.590 --> 35:34.590
with the air of a bandit king.

632
35:35.800 --> 35:38.280
Next, please enjoy the song and dance,

633
35:38.510 --> 35:39.760
Tea Lanterns Welcoming Spring!

634
35:38.530 --> 35:40.680
[Li Bozhao, President of the Gorky Drama School]

635
35:39.780 --> 35:42.610
Therefore, I plan to request Comrade Wang Ming

636
35:43.030 --> 35:46.400
to send Mao to Moscow

637
35:46.760 --> 35:49.760
for a period of serious study.

638
35:50.060 --> 35:52.770
I heard he's recently been reading

639
35:52.790 --> 35:54.860
Left-Wing Communism: An Infantile Disorder.

640
35:54.860 --> 35:56.710
Going to the birthplace of Leninism

641
35:56.710 --> 35:59.840
and the October Revolution to read it

642
35:59.840 --> 36:03.030
would be most fitting.

643
36:04.510 --> 36:06.840
You must understand,

644
36:07.190 --> 36:11.480
I came to China without any personal selfish motives.

645
36:11.500 --> 36:13.090
I am here to help you apply

646
36:13.120 --> 36:15.000
the great Soviet-style tactics

647
36:15.000 --> 36:16.880
to achieve victory.

648
36:17.320 --> 36:18.400
Comrade Li De,

649
36:18.400 --> 36:21.950
I have never doubted that.

650
36:22.150 --> 36:25.760
I will continue to support you as always.

651
36:26.110 --> 36:28.440
Great!

652
36:43.810 --> 36:46.460
Great!

653
36:50.280 --> 36:55.190
Great!

654
36:58.440 --> 37:00.450
Next, please enjoy

655
37:00.480 --> 37:01.960
the Sabre Dance!

656
37:01.980 --> 37:04.130
Okay.

657
37:07.880 --> 37:09.280
I'll go find Comrade Zedong.

658
37:09.280 --> 37:09.960
Okay.

659
37:12.550 --> 37:14.760
Mom, I want to see the dragon dance!

660
37:14.960 --> 37:17.290
You want to see the dragon dance? Let's go.

661
37:17.840 --> 37:20.000
Dad is coming too!

662
37:20.000 --> 37:20.510
Okay.

663
37:20.510 --> 37:21.760
Let's go together.

664
37:21.760 --> 37:24.000
Great!

665
37:24.000 --> 37:25.190
Comrade Zedong.

666
37:26.630 --> 37:27.560
Comrade Zizhen.

667
37:28.150 --> 37:29.160
Comrade Enlai.

668
37:29.310 --> 37:30.040
Maomao.

669
37:30.070 --> 37:30.840
Say hello.

670
37:30.200 --> 37:32.030
[Maomao, son of Mao Zedong]

671
37:31.110 --> 37:31.880
Hello!

672
37:32.840 --> 37:35.960
Great!

673
37:36.550 --> 37:39.230
Comrade Enlai, what can I do for you?

674
37:40.760 --> 37:42.020
Let's talk over there.

675
37:43.550 --> 37:45.840
♪ Fearing no death, loving no wealth ♪

676
37:45.840 --> 37:48.070
♪ Let us all strive to march forward ♪

677
37:48.070 --> 37:49.510
♪ Strive on, strive on ♪

678
37:49.510 --> 37:51.150
♪ Fight, onward to the fight ♪

679
37:52.360 --> 37:54.690
Send the telegram as quickly as possible.

680
37:56.280 --> 37:56.710
Okay.

681
37:56.710 --> 37:57.710
Catch it!

682
37:58.670 --> 38:00.800
Awesome!

683
38:02.070 --> 38:03.280
The Central Committee has decided

684
38:03.280 --> 38:06.220
you will no longer serve as Chairman of the Council of People's Commissars.

685
38:06.220 --> 38:07.880
Comrade Luofu will take over.

686
38:07.900 --> 38:09.640
You will focus solely on being Chairman

687
38:09.640 --> 38:12.100
of the Soviet Central Executive Committee.

688
38:15.110 --> 38:18.400
They still leave

689
38:18.430 --> 38:19.740
such a title to me.

690
38:20.480 --> 38:21.000
I am deeply grateful.

691
38:21.000 --> 38:22.880
♪ If you join the army, join the Red Army ♪

692
38:23.550 --> 38:24.710
About this decision...

693
38:24.710 --> 38:26.850
♪ Officers and soldiers are all the same ♪

694
38:26.880 --> 38:28.840
♪ No one oppresses anyone ♪

695
38:28.940 --> 38:30.970
♪ If you join the army, join the Red Army ♪

696
38:31.000 --> 38:33.540
♪ Workers and peasants unite to kill the enemy ♪

697
38:32.000 --> 38:32.960
I'm very sorry.

698
38:33.110 --> 38:36.110
This has nothing to do with you. Don't blame yourself.

699
38:36.440 --> 38:38.230
The government is a massive undertaking.

700
38:38.230 --> 38:40.150
It's not bad to hand it over to Comrade Luofu.

701
38:40.150 --> 38:41.210
He has the ability.

702
38:41.590 --> 38:44.280
After all, a figurehead like me

703
38:44.800 --> 38:46.630
has outlived his usefulness.

704
38:48.710 --> 38:50.110
You're taking this quite calmly.

705
38:50.110 --> 38:51.920
Too much debt, you stop worrying.

706
38:51.920 --> 38:54.250
Too many lice, you stop feeling the bites.

707
38:55.030 --> 38:55.880
Since 1931,

708
38:56.480 --> 38:58.540
they started criticizing me in southern Jiangxi.

709
38:58.540 --> 39:00.110
First, after the Ningdu Meeting,

710
39:00.110 --> 39:03.150
they removed me as General Commissar of the First Red Army Group.

711
39:03.150 --> 39:07.480
Now, they're replacing me as Chairman of the Council of People's Commissars.

712
39:07.750 --> 39:08.940
On the Fifth Plenary Session of the Sixth Central Committee,

713
39:08.940 --> 39:10.110
they even pinned on me

714
39:10.110 --> 39:11.910
the label of right opportunism.

715
39:12.190 --> 39:14.040
The list goes on and on.

716
39:14.120 --> 39:15.980
What's there not to be calm about?

717
39:18.110 --> 39:21.550
I'm like a foul-smelling rock in a latrine.

718
39:21.740 --> 39:23.600
They all treat me like the plague.

719
39:24.090 --> 39:25.760
Even ghosts won't come near my door.

720
39:25.760 --> 39:28.230
Comrade Enlai, you talk so much to me.

721
39:29.000 --> 39:30.600
Careful not to get infected.

722
39:31.840 --> 39:33.400
I won't get infected.

723
39:33.800 --> 39:36.330
The Fifth Plenary Session had one more label:

724
39:36.480 --> 39:38.030
a conciliatory attitude

725
39:38.030 --> 39:39.560
toward right opportunism.

726
39:40.030 --> 39:40.840
Who got that one?

727
39:40.840 --> 39:41.590
Me.

728
39:45.400 --> 39:46.590
What are you doing?

729
39:46.760 --> 39:47.920
Why are you hitting other people?

730
39:47.920 --> 39:48.510
He's hitting someone!

731
39:48.510 --> 39:49.500
If you hit people, get off the stage!

732
39:49.500 --> 39:50.760
Comrades, we're just acting in a play!

733
39:50.760 --> 39:51.510
Calm down!

734
39:51.920 --> 39:57.360
Comrade Zedong, people may hand out labels,

735
39:57.630 --> 40:00.400
but the work still needs to be done.

736
40:00.530 --> 40:02.780
We fought for our common ideals

737
40:02.810 --> 40:04.340
to get to where we are today.

738
40:04.480 --> 40:06.480
Reaching this stage

739
40:06.960 --> 40:07.690
wasn't easy.

740
40:08.230 --> 40:11.560
We can't just passively walk off the stage halfway through.

741
40:14.400 --> 40:16.510
Comrade Enlai, you worry too much.

742
40:18.400 --> 40:22.130
Owning not half an acre of land, yet worrying about the whole world.

743
40:22.320 --> 40:24.510
I will never change.

744
40:25.690 --> 40:27.960
Keep the big picture in mind, and work together for the Party.

745
40:27.960 --> 40:29.960
Who said those words?

746
40:30.480 --> 40:33.190
I said them to you after the Ningdu Meeting.

747
40:35.400 --> 40:39.070
I share these words with you now, for mutual encouragement.

748
40:42.820 --> 40:43.950
Tomorrow, I will finish

749
40:43.950 --> 40:46.510
Conclusions on the Report of the Central Executive Committee

750
40:46.510 --> 40:48.150
and submit it.

751
40:52.030 --> 40:53.850
Long live the Red Army!

752
40:53.880 --> 40:56.540
Long live the Red Army!

753
40:56.630 --> 40:58.850
Long live the Communist Party of China!

754
40:58.870 --> 41:02.200
Long live the Communist Party of China!

755
41:02.230 --> 41:05.270
[Eastern Front Defensive Positions, Central Soviet Area]

756
41:04.840 --> 41:07.900
Just as the Second National Soviet Congress convened,

757
41:07.970 --> 41:09.260
the main Nationalist force

758
41:09.260 --> 41:10.730
suppressed the People's Revolutionary Government

759
41:10.730 --> 41:13.580
organized by the 19th Route Army in Fuzhou.

760
41:14.510 --> 41:18.480
It mobilized four armies from the east, north, west, and south

761
41:18.480 --> 41:20.540
to encircle the Central Soviet Area.

762
41:20.960 --> 41:21.890
Following that,

763
41:22.030 --> 41:24.150
from the two main directions of the east and north,

764
41:24.150 --> 41:26.150
they launched focused offensives.

765
41:26.670 --> 41:28.140
Facing this critical situation,

766
41:28.140 --> 41:30.540
Bo Gu, Li De, and others in military command

767
41:30.880 --> 41:32.320
ordered the Central Red Army

768
41:32.320 --> 41:34.000
to fight blockhouse against blockhouse

769
41:34.000 --> 41:35.800
and use short, swift thrust tactics,

770
41:35.800 --> 41:38.630
engaging the enemy outside the borders.

771
41:38.630 --> 41:41.280
Despite the Red Army commanders and fighters braving death

772
41:41.280 --> 41:42.880
and fighting tenaciously,

773
41:42.880 --> 41:45.320
under the enemy's fierce offensives,

774
41:45.510 --> 41:48.590
the defense lines were repeatedly pushed back.

775
42:36.760 --> 42:37.630
Comrades,

776
42:37.840 --> 42:40.190
this Monument to the Red Army Martyrs

777
42:40.400 --> 42:42.600
was built brick by brick with donations

778
42:42.670 --> 42:45.070
from the people of the Central Soviet Area.

779
42:45.110 --> 42:47.770
Comrade Qian Zhuangfei designed this monument

780
42:48.180 --> 42:50.110
in the shape of an artillery shell.

781
42:50.230 --> 42:53.070
I think it holds deep meaning.

782
42:53.360 --> 42:54.630
From the Nanchang Uprising,

783
42:54.630 --> 42:56.400
the Autumn Harvest and Guangzhou Uprisings,

784
42:56.400 --> 42:58.810
to dozens of uprisings across the country,

785
42:59.010 --> 43:01.470
the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army

786
43:01.550 --> 43:04.000
has smashed multiple enemy encirclement campaigns.
